Impact: Having a minimum lvlUSDAmount of 0 exposes the receiver / collateral provider to a maximum
slippage risk in terms of minted lvlUSD vs. provided collateral, which can turn out to be a severe loss.
Likelihood: The lvlUSD token has 18 decimals which is most common for ERC20 tokens. Despite
USDC/USDT having only 6 decimals on Ethereum, it is not unlikely that another stablecoin with 18 decimals
will be used as collateral.
