5.1.1    Protocol fees are double-counted as registry balance and pool reserve
Severity: Critical Risk
Context: Portfolio.sol#L489-L507
Description: When swapping, the registry is credited a protocolFee. However, this fee is always reinvested in the
pool, meaning the virtualX or virtualY pool reserves per liquidity increase by protocolFee / liquidity. The
protocol fee is now double-counted as the registry’s user balance and the pool reserve, while the global reserves
are only increased by the protocol fee once in _increaseReserves(_state.tokenInput, iteration.input). A
protocol fee breaks the invariant that the global reserve should be greater than the sum of user balances and fees
plus the sum of pool reserves.
As the protocol fee is reinvested, LPs can withdraw them. If users and LPs decide to withdraw all their balances,
the registry can’t withdraw their fees anymore. Conversely, if the registry withdraws the protocol fee, not all users
can withdraw their balances anymore.
// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
